                <pb facs="0140" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.61/66: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-18T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>77. Recent reports indicate that trains of ammunition presumably bought by Polish
                    Government have been held in Czechoslovakia. <pb facs="0141" n="43"
                        xml:id="pg43"/> You are instructed to very discreetly obtain facts.
                    Department’s information is not sufficiently full to warrant direct
                    inquiries.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
